 "id": "4.1",
 "chapter": "4",
 "title": "The slowly-varying envelope approximation",
 "short": "Slowly-varying envelope",
 "lead": "How light propagating through a medium of atoms is described: the <span data-concept=\"wave-equation-with-polarization\">wave equation</span> with the atoms’ <span data-concept=\"macroscopic-polarization\">polarization</span> as its source, and the <span data-concept=\"slowly-varying-envelope-approximation\">slowly-varying envelope approximation</span>, which writes the field and polarization as envelopes on a carrier and gives a propagation equation for the envelope, for a single carrier and for the harmonics of an <span data-concept=\"optical-frequency-comb\">optical frequency comb</span>.",
