 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "c-eq-4-28",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book writes $\\kkbar$ in both coefficients for every harmonic. Each harmonic carries its own wavevector $k_n = \\knu_n/c$, the $nk$ of Eq. (4.26), so the equation for $\\kEenv_n$ reads $\\frac{1}{2ik_n}\\nabla_\\perp^2\\kEenv_n + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}\\kEenv_n + \\frac{1}{c}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial \\kt}\\kEenv_n = \\frac{ik_n}{2\\epsilon_0}\\kPenv_n$; with $\\kkbar$ it holds only while the comb’s bandwidth is small beside $\\knubar$, not for arbitrarily short pulses."
  }
 ],
